        Phrase("J'espère que tu vas bien", "I hope you're well", "Natumai uko vizuri", "Natumai uko poa", "Friendly-letter health check.", "espérer que + INDICATIVE (hope as fact): J'espère que tu vas bien. Contrast vouloir que + subj.", "A2"),
        Phrase("Je t'embrasse très fort", "Big hugs", "Nakukumbatia sana", null, "Warm amicale sign-off.", "Sign-off ladder amicale: Bises / Je t'embrasse / Grosses bises. Never in formelle.", "A2"),
        Phrase("P.S. : n'oublie pas les photos", "P.S.: don't forget the photos", "P.S.: usisahau picha", null, "Post-scriptum shows real letter habits.", "P.S. = post-scriptum. Examiners smile: it proves you know letter culture, not just templates.", "A2"),
        Phrase("Je vous écris pour postuler", "I'm writing to apply", "Nawaandikia kuomba kazi", null, "Purpose in sentence one.", "écrire pour + infinitive. State the post: …au poste de caissier, suite à votre annonce du 3 mai.", "B1")
    ), "u8"),
    Lesson("k-redaction", "🖊️", "Rédaction", "Composition plan & connectors", "Insha", listOf(
        Phrase("Tout d'abord, définissons le sujet", "First, let's define the topic", "Kwanza, tufafanue mada", null, "Introduction: reformulate the subject, announce plan.", "Intro formula: sujet + problématique + annonce du plan (d'abord, ensuite, enfin). Three sentences.", "B1", true),
        Phrase("D'une part, c'est utile", "On one hand, it's useful", "Kwa upande mmoja, ni muhimu", null, "Balanced argument scaffold.", "D'une part… d'autre part… — the KCSE essay skeleton. Examiners scan for it.", "B1"),
        Phrase("En revanche, ça coûte cher", "On the other hand, it's expensive", "Kwa upande mwingine, ni ghali", null, "en revanche = contrast, stronger than mais.", "Connector ladder: mais < cependant < en revanche < néanmoins. Climb it through the essay.", "B1"),
        Phrase("Par exemple, à Kibera", "For example, in Kibera", "Kwa mfano, Kibera", "For example, Kibera", "Examples must be CONCRETE: places, numbers, names.", "Par exemple + proper noun + detail beats abstract claims. 'À Kisumu, le marché…' = marks.", "A2"),
        Phrase("De plus, ça crée des emplois", "Moreover, it creates jobs", "Zaidi ya hayo, inazalisha ajira", null, "de plus adds arguments. Never start two paragraphs with it.", "Addition ladder: d'abord, ensuite, de plus, enfin. One per paragraph, in order.", "B1"),
        Phrase("Pourtant, rien ne change", "Yet nothing changes", "Lakini, hakuna kinachobadilika", null, "pourtant = concession punch.", "Pourtant / cependant concede then strike: Tout le monde promet, pourtant… Strong middle-paragraph move.", "B1"),
        Phrase("En conclusion, je propose que", "In conclusion, I propose that", "Kwa hitimisho, napendekeza kwamba", null, "Conclusion: opinion + proposal, no new arguments.", "Conclusion formula: bilan (en somme) + avis (à mon avis) + ouverture (il faudrait que + subjunctive).", "B1"),
        Phrase("Il faudrait que l'État agisse", "The state should act", "Serikali inapaswa kuchukua hatua", null, "il faudrait que + SUBJUNCTIVE. B2 flex in a B1 essay.", "il faut que / il faudrait que → subjunctive: agisse, fasse, prenne. One subjunctive = examiner smile.", "B2"),
        Phrase("À mon avis, c'est injuste", "In my opinion, it's unfair", "Kwa maoni yangu, si haki", "Kwa maoni yangu, si fair", "à mon avis announces YOUR voice.", "Opinion markers: à mon avis, selon moi, pour ma part. Required at least once in discursive essays.", "A2"),
        Phrase("Cent cinquante mots environ", "About 150 words", "Maneno mia na hamsini hivi", null, "Respect the word count ±10%.", "Count lines × ~10 words. Too short = penalized; too long = errors multiply. Plan 15–18 lines.", "A2"),
        Phrase("D'abord, ensuite, enfin", "First, then, finally", "Kwanza, kisha, mwisho", null, "The plan skeleton in three words.", "Announce the plan in the intro, then obey it. Examiners check intro vs body match.", "A2"),
